# VTID-03770 — commands run during investigation and verification

## Investigation (read-only, live oasis_events tracing via Supabase MCP)

Allocated VTID and set title/status:
  SELECT allocate_global_vtid('claude-code', 'DEV', 'orb-guided-topic');
  UPDATE vtid_ledger SET title=..., status='in_progress', spec_status='approved' WHERE vtid='VTID-03770';

Scoped to the documented e2e test account first — a dead end, corrected by
widening scope rather than trusting it:
  SELECT ... FROM oasis_events WHERE created_at > now() - interval '3 hours'
    AND (actor_id = 'a27552a3-...' OR metadata->>'user_id' = 'a27552a3-...')
  SELECT ... WHERE metadata::text ILIKE '%guided_topic%' AND user_id = 'a27552a3-...'
    -- zero rows in the last 12 hours; ruled this account out.

Widened to all users/all guided-topic activity in the last 6 hours:
  SELECT ... WHERE metadata::text ILIKE '%guided_topic%' OR message ILIKE '%guided%'
    -- found the real reporting account bc34a5ca-6966-44f6-9507-3bed98e3e1d5
       (j.tadic@exafy.io), topics T003 (08:01) and T005 (09:15).

Full second-by-second trace of the T005 session chain:
  SELECT created_at, topic, status, message, metadata FROM oasis_events
    WHERE created_at > '2026-08-27 09:14:00+00'
      AND (metadata->>'user_id' = 'bc34a5ca-...'
        OR metadata->>'session_id' = 'live-c3bde79b-371a-4bf9-8349-bcfe1b9b573a')
    ORDER BY created_at ASC;
  -- traced: live-c3bde79b (nova_validation x2, superseded) ->
  --         live-3b5251dd (real 37.7s/335-chunk teaching turn, connection drop) ->
  --         live-4c56c1f3 (generic reopen, all_sources_skipped, ~4.5s, hide)

Static code reading (services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js):
  grep -n "setInterval|_reconnectTimer|..." orb-widget.js
    -> found _s._recoveryWatchdog (5s health-probe, line ~1361) and
       _s._guidedTopicBackstopInterval (VTID-03762, unrelated to this bug).
  Read _resetAndReconnect() in full (lines 1437-1484) — confirmed NO
    reference to _guidedTopicInFlight anywhere in its body, unlike
    _attemptReconnect() (lines 4269-4370), which has the VTID-03746 guard.
  Read _hide() (confirms _guidedTopicInFlight is cleared ONLY there),
    focusGuidedTopic (confirms it's set ONLY there), and the turn-complete
    handler (confirms it deliberately does NOT clear _guidedTopicInFlight,
    only _s.guidedTopic — the VTID-03746 design).
  Read guided-topic-narration.ts (server-side provider) — confirmed its
    candidate decision is a pure function of whether guided_topic_id
    arrived on the request; no server-side dedup/already-delivered gate
    that would explain the missing candidate independent of the client.
  grep -n "superseded_by_new_session" across services/gateway/src —
    confirmed this is the server killing an existing tracked-active session
    when a NEW session-start request arrives for the same user
    (routes/orb-live.ts).
  grep -n "closeBtn|pointer-events" orb-widget.js — confirmed the close
    button is created once (idempotent _renderOverlay guard) and bound
    directly to _hide with no state-based disabling; ruled out a DOM/
    z-index explanation for "close doesn't react."

## Implementation

Edit to services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/orb-widget.js,
_resetAndReconnect():
  - Changed `_s._isReconnecting = false;` to `_s._isReconnecting = true;`
    at function entry.
  - Added the guided-topic restore guard (identical shape to
    _attemptReconnect()'s) immediately before `_sessionStart()`.
  - Added `_s._isReconnecting = false;` to both the `.then()` success
    branch and the `.catch()` failure branch.

